course: dictionary
lesson: 3184
title: A word borrowed from French
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words travel from one language to another and keep their shape. Encore is a French word that is used in English. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «An encore is an extra song after the show seems finished» tells you what it means at a concert.
explain: When the audience claps and wants more, the band plays one more song. Encore can also be shouted on its own, as in «Encore!», which means "more, please!" The same word can be a thing in one sentence and a shout in another.
explain: The French word means again, or still. Try the French meaning in the sentence to check it. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Encore is a noun for an extra song at the end of a concert.
fact: «Encore!» is shouted by an audience to ask for more.
fact: Encore comes from French and means again.
fact: Big bands often plan their encore in advance, as «most big bands plan it in advance» shows.
fact: French audiences shout «Bis!» where English audiences shout «Encore!»
exercise: «The band played one encore before they left the stage.» What is an encore here? | A quiet rest between two songs | A ticket for the bus home | *An extra song played because the audience wants more | A kind of drum
exercise: The crowd shouted «Encore!» What were they asking for? | A bigger stage | A refund | *More, please | Silence
exercise: In French, encore means what? | Goodbye | Very loud | *Again or still | Ten
test: «The singer agreed to do an encore after the clapping went on and on.» What does do an encore mean here? | Sing the first song again by mistake | Leave the stage early | *Play an extra song | Stop the concert for a break
test: Why did the audience shout «Encore!»? | To ask for the lights to go off | To warn the band | *Because they wanted more | To say goodbye
exam: Jayden says encore is only a French word, so it must be a shout. What is the best answer? | No, it can be a noun for an extra song, and it means again in French | No, it is not a real word | *No, it can be a noun for an extra song, and it can also be a shout | Yes, it is only ever shouted
